SUMMARY
-------
Native SwiftUI implementation of the web TripReplay page, adaptive across macOS +
iOS/iPadOS (ADR-002/006). A `@State TripReplayPageModel` (`@Observable`, P1/S8 seam)
owns the `useDrive(id)` query + the single playhead index threaded through the map,
scrubber, current-position stats, elevation profile, speed+power timeline, and drive
summary. SI is converted only at the display boundary (P1/S5 converters reproduced
in TripReplayUnitMath); every string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings (verbatim
web `replay.*` keys); every color/font is a P2 design token.

FILES (apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Trips/)
  TripReplayPage.swift             — adaptive page View + scaffold + 4-state switch
  TripReplayPage.Types.swift       — SI value inputs + load/connection/update + phase + tiles
  TripReplayPage.Model.swift       — @Observable model + source seam + InMemory source + Strings
  TripReplayPage.Projection.swift  — pure projection (tiles / phase / charts / playhead timing)
  TripReplayPage.Format.swift      — SI→display converters + fmt + duration + haversine
  TripReplayPage.Views.swift       — freshness chip, banner, current-stats panel, summary panel
  TripReplayPage.Sections.swift    — route map, playback bar, elevation, timeline
  TripReplayPage.States.swift      — loading / empty / error data states
  TripReplayPage.Navigation.swift  — TripReplayRoute + deep-link parser + navigationDestination
  TripReplayPage.Previews.swift    — content/empty/loading/error/stale/offline × metric/imperial
  TripReplayPage.Tests.swift       — projection + model + deep-link XCTest
Integration: project.yml (TeslaSync/Features registered in iOS + macOS app targets),
  .swiftlint.yml (Features included), Localization/Localizable.xcstrings (+37 keys).

